WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.095
(applause)

00:00:01.095 --> 00:00:05.010
- It's been 30 years since
Billboard ranked "Hold On"

00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:06.340
Song of the Year.

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:09.550
Was there a time in your life that you,

00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:12.410
kind of exactly on point, and
needed to hear that message?

00:00:12.410 --> 00:00:13.243
- Oh, yeah.

00:00:13.243 --> 00:00:14.235
- Yeah.

00:00:14.235 --> 00:00:15.196
- Yeah.

00:00:15.196 --> 00:00:16.029
- Yeah.

00:00:16.029 --> 00:00:18.670
- No, I was really in a dark, dark space

00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:20.693
when that lyric was written.

00:00:20.693 --> 00:00:24.390
I was really at a point in
my life where I felt like

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:26.870
if I was at a crossroads,
and I really felt like

00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:28.770
if I didn't get my life together and

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:32.300
stop doing a little drugs and

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:36.227
had a really bad boyfriend at the time.

00:00:36.227 --> 00:00:38.676
I just was in a lot of
pain and I just said,

00:00:38.676 --> 00:00:42.347
"If I don't change my course, I'm gonna be

00:00:42.347 --> 00:00:43.560
"in a lotta trouble."

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:45.820
So I knew that I was at
a crossroads and that I

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:48.450
either had to like, hold
on for one more day or just

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:49.283
die.

00:00:49.283 --> 00:00:50.116
(laughs)

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:51.020
- Can I thank you for
being honest about that?

00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:53.401
'Cause not everybody is honest about that.

00:00:53.401 --> 00:00:56.470
- I'm sober 15 years and, you know,

00:00:56.470 --> 00:01:00.470
I was gonna say I need it now
in this world, in this time.

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:02.550
You need, you know, inspiration like this

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:05.100
and songs that can help get
you through it, you know?

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:05.933
So I need it now.

00:01:05.933 --> 00:01:06.766
- [Kelly] Music heals.

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:08.078
- Music heals.

00:01:08.078 --> 00:01:09.020
For sure.

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:11.090
- So what are your like, favorite memories

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:13.040
from the time it hit number one?

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:14.450
Like, did you splurge?

00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:16.540
Or did you do something
fantastic, perform somewhere

00:01:16.540 --> 00:01:18.164
that was just like--

00:01:18.164 --> 00:01:19.130
- The first time I heard
it it was on my birthday

00:01:19.130 --> 00:01:19.963
on the radio.

00:01:19.963 --> 00:01:22.710
The first time I heard "Hold
On" was on my birthday.

00:01:22.710 --> 00:01:23.543
- [Kelly] That's a gift.

00:01:23.543 --> 00:01:24.668
- What a great gift that was.

00:01:24.668 --> 00:01:25.672
- Wow!

00:01:25.672 --> 00:01:27.156
- We were in Tennessee
in a van, I remember--

00:01:27.156 --> 00:01:27.989
- Yes, we were!

00:01:27.989 --> 00:01:30.110
- I remember all the details.

00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:31.175
I swear to God.

00:01:31.175 --> 00:01:32.008
- How do you remember that?

00:01:32.008 --> 00:01:32.940
- I don't know.

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:35.340
I was terrible in school,
I have no clue why.

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:37.080
- I know, I retained nothing.

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:39.820
- But the dates and
stuff like that is weird.

00:01:39.820 --> 00:01:42.470
But just knowing that we were so young

00:01:42.470 --> 00:01:44.150
when this happened, you know,

00:01:44.150 --> 00:01:45.530
we were on the whirlwind on tour,

00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:46.820
we were just, we didn't know anything

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:49.200
except we were a group, we loved to sing,

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:51.760
and we just were embraced by the world

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:53.910
and we're grateful for that, you know?

00:01:53.910 --> 00:01:55.170
- [Women] Amen.

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:56.119
- Lotta hard work.

00:01:56.119 --> 00:01:57.340
- So, like--

00:01:57.340 --> 00:01:59.060
okay, you just said something interesting

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.910
and I confessed this
when we were rehearsing,

00:02:00.910 --> 00:02:03.140
but I had no idea--

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:04.950
everyone make fun of me now--

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:08.042
I had no idea who your parents were.

00:02:08.042 --> 00:02:09.000
(laughter)

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:10.040
- Not everybody does.

00:02:10.040 --> 00:02:11.713
- Until last night.

00:02:13.241 --> 00:02:14.610
Until last night.

00:02:14.610 --> 00:02:15.443
I was like,

00:02:15.443 --> 00:02:17.157
"Why do they keep talking
about The Mamas and The Papas

00:02:17.157 --> 00:02:18.624
"and the Beach Boys?"

00:02:18.624 --> 00:02:19.457
I was like,

00:02:19.457 --> 00:02:20.290
"I love The Mamas and the Papas,"

00:02:20.290 --> 00:02:21.123
I was like,

00:02:21.123 --> 00:02:21.956
"What does this have to do?"

00:02:21.956 --> 00:02:22.789
And I was like,

00:02:22.789 --> 00:02:23.622
"What?"

00:02:23.622 --> 00:02:24.455
I was like--

00:02:24.455 --> 00:02:25.850
I had no idea like, I just
want you to know like on your--

00:02:25.850 --> 00:02:26.683
- We take that as a compliment!

00:02:26.683 --> 00:02:28.510
- On your own merit, I was a fan.

00:02:28.510 --> 00:02:31.920
It had nothing to do with
parents or anything and

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:33.280
I think that that's kind of something.

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:35.750
'Cause like to grow up, and I imagine that

00:02:35.750 --> 00:02:36.583
was very hard.

00:02:36.583 --> 00:02:38.340
I'm gauging that and
navigating that with my kids,

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:40.940
I'm sure you have to as well,
but being in the public eye,

00:02:40.940 --> 00:02:44.550
having parents so famous
and trying to navigate that

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:46.150
and like, what is normal?

00:02:46.150 --> 00:02:47.600
And how do I...

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:48.433
- [Chynna] There was no normal.

00:02:48.433 --> 00:02:50.033
- It's so hard.

00:02:50.033 --> 00:02:51.248
- There was no normal.
- That was our normal.

00:02:51.248 --> 00:02:53.030
The chaos.
- right, right.

00:02:53.030 --> 00:02:54.814
- [Kelly] I know, that's not good.

00:02:54.814 --> 00:02:55.647
(laughter)

00:02:55.647 --> 00:02:57.046
- Well, but it was exciting too.

00:02:57.046 --> 00:02:58.030
- Says my therapist.

00:02:58.030 --> 00:02:58.863
- Yeah, right.

00:02:59.824 --> 00:03:01.490
But we also have a great mom, Marilyn,

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:02.850
who's in the audience today.

00:03:02.850 --> 00:03:04.134
Our mother Marilyn.

00:03:04.134 --> 00:03:06.223
But she was really,

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:09.980
she was really great at
keeping it, you know, steady

00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:11.690
and being real about things, you know?

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:14.010
Not everything is normal
or what is normal?

00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:16.500
And you know, building
our self esteem as people

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:18.160
and showing us love.

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:20.380
And now we instill that in our kids.

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:21.300
- Yeah.

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:22.133
- [Carnie] It's important.

00:03:22.133 --> 00:03:23.250
- It's a weird thing to navigate.

00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:24.220
But like, I know...

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:26.730
So since finding that
out and I kind of read

00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:27.880
in a thing like,

00:03:27.880 --> 00:03:30.784
one of you was put to
bed by Sir Elton John,

00:03:30.784 --> 00:03:33.187
and I was like,

00:03:33.187 --> 00:03:34.047
"What?"

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:36.303
What is your life?

00:03:37.457 --> 00:03:38.504
That's insane.

00:03:38.504 --> 00:03:39.690
What was he doing at your house?

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:40.640
- He told you a lullaby or something?

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:41.858
I don't get it, what?

00:03:41.858 --> 00:03:42.691
- No, no, no.

00:03:42.691 --> 00:03:44.120
He reminded me when I was

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:47.697
just on "The Talk" with him
a couple years ago that,

00:03:47.697 --> 00:03:48.530
"Don't you remember?

00:03:48.530 --> 00:03:49.640
"I put you to sleep."

00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:50.473
And I'm like,

00:03:50.473 --> 00:03:51.580
"What?"

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:52.413
- I'd be like,

00:03:52.413 --> 00:03:53.246
"No, but I'm telling everyone."

00:03:53.246 --> 00:03:54.340
- Yeah, exactly!

00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:55.173
He literally--

00:03:55.173 --> 00:03:57.550
I mean, he just wanted to buy Dad's piano

00:03:57.550 --> 00:04:00.310
that Dad wrote "Good Vibrations" on.

00:04:00.310 --> 00:04:01.405
That was his mission.

00:04:01.405 --> 00:04:02.370
- [Kelly] Solid piano.
- Solid piano.

00:04:02.370 --> 00:04:04.770
Lot of memories there
and he wanted this piano.

00:04:04.770 --> 00:04:06.700
He came over and he was
probably begging for it.

00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:07.840
My mom said no.

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:10.130
But he, I guess I came
downstairs and they were

00:04:10.130 --> 00:04:11.407
chatting and doing
their thing and he said,

00:04:11.407 --> 00:04:12.550
"Time to go back to bed,"

00:04:12.550 --> 00:04:14.430
and put me in my bed and that was

00:04:14.430 --> 00:04:15.340
Elton John putting me to sleep.

00:04:15.340 --> 00:04:16.378
- Okay, the best...

00:04:16.378 --> 00:04:18.810
The best part, it turns out, of this story

00:04:18.810 --> 00:04:20.400
actually isn't that, it's the fact

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:21.233
that your mom was like,

00:04:21.233 --> 00:04:22.370
"No, you can't have our piano.

00:04:22.370 --> 00:04:23.810
- [Carnie] I know!

00:04:23.810 --> 00:04:24.790
- To Elton John!

00:04:24.790 --> 00:04:25.790
- I know.

00:04:25.790 --> 00:04:26.623
Well guess what,

00:04:26.623 --> 00:04:28.876
that piano's mine now
so I'm very, very happy.

00:04:28.876 --> 00:04:30.840
(audience cheering)

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:32.809
She said I could have it!
- She said hey!

00:04:32.809 --> 00:04:34.410
- Wendy.
- Thanks, Mom.

00:04:34.410 --> 00:04:35.470
- Thanks, Mom, great.

00:04:35.470 --> 00:04:37.240
So what are you working on now?

00:04:37.240 --> 00:04:38.600
You said you do a show a month,

00:04:38.600 --> 00:04:41.066
like everybody can find you
doing a show but what all,

00:04:41.066 --> 00:04:42.440
I know you each have kinda
different things you're into.

00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:44.160
- Yeah, so we do our one show a month

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:46.270
and I've got a YouTube
channel up right now,

00:04:46.270 --> 00:04:47.660
which I'm really super excited about

00:04:47.660 --> 00:04:49.680
called California Preaching

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:51.130
and it's all about--

00:04:51.130 --> 00:04:53.437
okay, I believe Jesus is the son of God.

00:04:53.437 --> 00:04:55.517
And so I talk a lot about Jesus.

00:04:55.517 --> 00:04:57.260
(audience applause)

00:04:57.260 --> 00:04:58.255
- That's amazing.

00:04:58.255 --> 00:04:59.750
So that's what you do
in California Preaching?

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:01.710
- California Preaching, Chynna Phillips,

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:03.400
California Preaching YouTube.

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:04.390
- Yeah, I love that.

00:05:04.390 --> 00:05:06.870
Passion is good, spirituality is great.

00:05:06.870 --> 00:05:07.703
- [Chynna] It is.

00:05:07.703 --> 00:05:08.793
- What are you up to, ma'am?

00:05:08.793 --> 00:05:10.890
- So I'm raising four boys.

00:05:10.890 --> 00:05:11.723
- Whew, girls.

00:05:12.667 --> 00:05:14.100
- That's a handful!

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:14.933
- Teenagers.

00:05:14.933 --> 00:05:17.734
- So I will be giving you
a lot of wine backstage.

00:05:17.734 --> 00:05:18.567
(laughter)

00:05:18.567 --> 00:05:20.058
- I need to start drinking wine.

00:05:20.058 --> 00:05:21.380
- Wendy!

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:22.213
- I'm just kidding.

00:05:22.213 --> 00:05:23.046
But

00:05:23.046 --> 00:05:24.130
I'm also trying to develop

00:05:24.130 --> 00:05:26.430
my own personal care products.

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:28.832
Line of personal care
so I'm working on that.

00:05:28.832 --> 00:05:29.665
- Are you really into
all the healthy things?

00:05:29.665 --> 00:05:30.660
I found that happened with me.

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:32.840
I never cared about me
but once I had kids,

00:05:32.840 --> 00:05:33.673
I was like,

00:05:33.673 --> 00:05:34.887
"What's in this?"

00:05:34.887 --> 00:05:36.740
It was like, you feel responsible.

00:05:36.740 --> 00:05:37.668
So that's amazing.

00:05:37.668 --> 00:05:38.501
- I was always that
way, I was always like,

00:05:38.501 --> 00:05:40.030
a health nut, you know, wanted to know

00:05:40.030 --> 00:05:41.350
the ingredients and stuff.

00:05:41.350 --> 00:05:43.180
But yeah, it's important to me, for sure.

00:05:43.180 --> 00:05:44.520
- It should be important to all of us.

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:45.580
Yeah, all right.

00:05:45.580 --> 00:05:46.950
- Yeah, and let's see what else.

00:05:46.950 --> 00:05:49.030
Well in terms of Wilson Phillips we just

00:05:49.030 --> 00:05:50.860
re-recorded "Hold On," it's
called "Hold On Today,"

00:05:50.860 --> 00:05:52.102
check it out on Spotify.

00:05:52.102 --> 00:05:53.111
- [Kelly] Awesome.

00:05:53.111 --> 00:05:54.119
(audience cheering)

00:05:54.119 --> 00:05:54.952
- Yeah, and...

00:05:54.952 --> 00:05:57.750
And I was gonna say that
Jesus does for you what

00:05:57.750 --> 00:05:59.920
pound cakes and cheesecakes do for me.

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:00.753
- Yes!

00:06:00.753 --> 00:06:03.410
- So I followed my heart and
my vision and I created--

00:06:03.410 --> 00:06:04.340
- It's my spirituality as well.

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:05.173
- That's right.

00:06:05.173 --> 00:06:07.572
And I created Love Bites by
Carnie, it's a nationwide--

00:06:07.572 --> 00:06:10.120
we're launching grocery this year.

00:06:10.120 --> 00:06:10.953
- That's amazing!
- It's a dessert line,

00:06:10.953 --> 00:06:11.786
a gourmet dessert.

00:06:11.786 --> 00:06:12.920
There's always a thing with the weight

00:06:12.920 --> 00:06:14.810
and the whole image but the truth is,

00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:17.240
I'm not giving up sugar, I'm
just gonna have a little bit

00:06:17.240 --> 00:06:19.130
and that's the message I think is healthy.

00:06:19.130 --> 00:06:20.209
(audience cheering)

00:06:20.209 --> 00:06:22.244
- No, I think it's a realistic thing.

00:06:22.244 --> 00:06:25.797
It's a realistic thing
for you to actually say,

00:06:25.797 --> 00:06:27.010
"Look, this is something I--"

00:06:27.010 --> 00:06:28.067
and for me, personally, I'm always like,

00:06:28.067 --> 00:06:29.447
"Look, I struggle with
this so I'm gonna allow

00:06:29.447 --> 00:06:30.938
"a little bit, like portion--"

00:06:30.938 --> 00:06:31.931
- That's healthy.

00:06:31.931 --> 00:06:32.764
- And try and stay, you
know, true the whole time.

00:06:32.764 --> 00:06:34.070
'Cause that's the only way
you'll be able to get there,

00:06:34.070 --> 00:06:34.903
I believe but.

00:06:34.903 --> 00:06:35.736
- [Carnie] It's realistic.

00:06:35.736 --> 00:06:37.164
- Yeah, anyway, I love cake.

00:06:37.164 --> 00:06:38.010
(laughter)

00:06:38.010 --> 00:06:39.440
So I got a video from you last night

00:06:39.440 --> 00:06:40.570
and I wanna show everybody the tape.

00:06:40.570 --> 00:06:41.770
It's awesome.

00:06:41.770 --> 00:06:43.310
- Okay, so Kelly,

00:06:43.310 --> 00:06:46.970
it's the day before the show,
the night before the show.

00:06:46.970 --> 00:06:48.920
I made peanut butter
cakes and then I heard

00:06:48.920 --> 00:06:51.070
that you didn't like peanut butter.

00:06:51.070 --> 00:06:52.470
So,

00:06:52.470 --> 00:06:55.980
I rushed back in the kitchen
and I made you lemon cakes.

00:06:55.980 --> 00:06:58.580
So here are your lemon cakes for tomorrow.

00:06:58.580 --> 00:06:59.880
Those are little bites.

00:06:59.880 --> 00:07:02.860
And I made you, I got some
beautiful frosting going.

00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:05.450
Some lemon marshmallow glaze.

00:07:05.450 --> 00:07:07.410
And I'm gonna glaze these
puppies and bring 'em in

00:07:07.410 --> 00:07:09.091
to you for tomorrow.

00:07:09.091 --> 00:07:10.818
- All right!

00:07:10.818 --> 00:07:11.821
So here we go.

00:07:11.821 --> 00:07:12.654
Would y'all like one?

00:07:12.654 --> 00:07:13.487
Would everybody like one?

00:07:13.487 --> 00:07:14.320
I'm gonna--

00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:15.153
well, I'll go first, fine.

00:07:15.153 --> 00:07:16.190
- Yeah, good.

00:07:16.190 --> 00:07:17.023
Go ahead.

00:07:17.023 --> 00:07:19.330
I've had five million of these
so I'll skip it right now.

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:20.720
- No, but I was gonna say though,

00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:22.390
if you do have a sweet
tooth, I think that this

00:07:22.390 --> 00:07:23.800
is amazing because--

00:07:23.800 --> 00:07:24.805
- [Carnie] Look at the size.

00:07:24.805 --> 00:07:25.800
- Yeah, the bite size.

00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:27.510
So it's like you're getting it
but it's not like excessive.

00:07:27.510 --> 00:07:28.756
- They're like my children.

00:07:28.756 --> 00:07:30.190
(laughter)

00:07:30.190 --> 00:07:31.940
- My problem is I get this at home

00:07:31.940 --> 00:07:33.663
and I don't eat just one.

00:07:33.663 --> 00:07:34.496
(laughter)

00:07:34.496 --> 00:07:35.329
- [Carnie] Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:07:35.329 --> 00:07:36.329
I know.
- Oh my gosh,

00:07:36.329 --> 00:07:37.322
these are so good!

00:07:37.322 --> 00:07:38.375
- Lemon, and it's lemon marshmallow.

00:07:38.375 --> 00:07:39.313
Hello!

00:07:40.540 --> 00:07:41.716
- [Kelly] You have mallow in it?

00:07:41.716 --> 00:07:42.776
Is that what you were gonna say?

00:07:42.776 --> 00:07:43.609
- Yeah, yeah, lemon marshmallow.

00:07:43.609 --> 00:07:44.824
- Oh my God, we are sisters
from a different mother.

00:07:44.824 --> 00:07:45.657
- I know.

00:07:45.657 --> 00:07:48.040
I'm definitely coming over,
we're baking together.

